course: dictionary
lesson: 7014
title: Parish: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Parish is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «A vicar or rector leads a Church of England parish.» A vicar or rector is a church leader, so here a parish must be an area that has its own church.
explain: Parish can also mean a small area, often a village, with its own local council. It can mean all the people who belong to a church, too. Ask yourself: is this about a place, a council, or a group of people? The clues will tell you which.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. If you say «the parish priest looks after the people of the area», it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A parish is an area that has its own church and priest or vicar, and the people who live there.
fact: In the UK, a parish can be a small area, often a village, with its own parish council.
fact: The parish can also mean all the people who belong to a church.
fact: Useful phrases: «parish church», «parish priest», «parish council» and «parish hall».
fact: In Louisiana, USA, a parish is like a county.
exercise: «A vicar or rector leads a Church of England parish.» What does parish mean here? | A priest's robe | A school for choir singers | *An area with its own church and the people who live there | A kind of church bell
exercise: A village has its own «parish council». What is a parish council? | A shop that sells candles | A group of people who sing in church | A court that judges crimes | *A small local council for an area, often a village
exercise: «The whole parish came to the summer fête.» What does parish mean in this sentence? | A prayer book | *All the people who belong to the church | A county in Louisiana | Only the church building
test: In Louisiana, USA, a parish is like what? | *A county | A church choir | A city park | A type of school
test: Which word completes «the ___ hall», a place where church groups meet? | village | *parish | castle | school
exam: Old «parish registers» list births and marriages. What does parish suggest here? | A type of cake | *An area with its own church and the people who live there | A kind of boat | A bird that sings
